#pragma once
// Moves mode (docs/moves-mode.md): checks that one launch's writes to a destination object are
// bitwise moves of a source object's units to the units a table names, over the memory-eliminated
// value IR. The moves term (schema sentryward.moves-term/v1) is input data generated by the caller
// from a `moves` clause of a kernel row's declaration.
//
// A match states, for every write to the destination object: it lies in the destination unit
// that the index table names for some source unit r (the table element at index.offset_bytes +
// r * index.stride_bytes), at the same offset in that unit as the bytes it copies in source unit
// r, and its value is those bytes of source unit r's initial contents, through loads, stores and
// same-width bitcasts only (no conversion, no arithmetic, no partial read). With live "none" (the
// table's elements are the excluded value under the input's premises) no write to the
// destination is allowed. A match is about this launch under the input's premises only.
#include <string>

#include "sentryward/value_analysis/memory_elimination.h"
#include "sentryward/value_analysis/unit_lifting.h"
#include "sentryward/value_ir/graph.h"

namespace sentryward::value_analysis {

// The JSON report (schema sentryward.moves-report/v1) of the moves check of `term_json` over
// `graph` after `memory`. Never throws on a term or graph mismatch: those are refusals in the
// report ("result": "matched" | "refused" | "unsupported"). Class mode (`lifting` not null) is
// unsupported: the check reads every CTA's writes.
std::string checkMovesTerm(const value_ir::Graph& graph, const MemoryEliminationResult& memory,
                           const std::string& term_json, const UnitLifting* lifting);

}  // namespace sentryward::value_analysis
